We have
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{O}_K\setminus \bigcup_{\mathfrak{s}\subset \mathcal{O}_K}\operatorname{Per}\nolimits(\eta,\mathfrak{s})=\mathcal{M}_{\mathfrak{D}}\cap \mathcal{F}_{\mathfrak{B}}=\mathcal{O}_K\setminus\bigcup_{i\geq1}\operatorname{Per}\nolimits(\eta,\mathfrak{s}_i),
\end{equation}
where $\mathfrak{D}$ is given by~(A), $(\mathfrak{s}_i)_{i\ge 1}$ is an ideal  filtration of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and summation is over all nonzero ideals $\mathfrak{s}\subseteq \mathcal{O}_K$.
